From 6fdf06800706f13004bee21eeab737eabfc86349 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Timo Derstappen <timo@giantswarm.io>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 20:07:41 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] fix(llmisvc): a workload with no available replica is not
 ready

Kubernetes reports a Deployment Available once at least replicas - maxUnavailable replicas are available. With spec.rolloutStrategy.maxUnavailable at or above the replica count (maxSurge: 0, maxUnavailable: 1 on a single replica, the strategy that lets a model filling its accelerator roll), that holds with zero replicas, so MainWorkloadReady and Ready turned true before any pod served and stayed true through every roll.

The workload's readiness now also requires an available replica whenever the Deployment desires any.

Signed-off-by: Timo Derstappen <timo@giantswarm.io>
---
 .../llmisvc/workload_readiness_test.go        | 61 +++++++++++++++++++
 .../v1alpha2/llmisvc/workload_single_node.go  | 40 ++++++++----
 2 files changed, 90 insertions(+), 11 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 pkg/controller/v1alpha2/llmisvc/workload_readiness_test.go

